Deloitte Cybersecurity Job Simulation::
 Task 1
📌 Task Title

Cyber Security – Investigating a Potential Breach

📖 Overview

This task simulates the role of a Cyber Security Analyst at Deloitte, where the objective was to investigate a suspected security breach involving Daikibo’s manufacturing status dashboard.

The investigation focused on analyzing web request logs to determine:

Whether an attacker could access the dashboard directly from the internet

Whether any suspicious or automated activity was present

Identifying the user ID most likely involved in abnormal behavior

🎯 Objectives

Determine if the alleged breach could originate from the internet without VPN access

Inspect web_requests.log for suspicious patterns

Identify abnormal request behavior

Pinpoint the most suspicious authorized user ID



🛠️ Tools & Resources Used

web_requests.log (internal dashboard access logs)

Deloitte-provided “How to Read the Logs” PDF

Manual log analysis using cybersecurity fundamentals

🧠 How I Completed the Task (Step-by-Step)
1️⃣ Understanding the Environment

Confirmed that Daikibo’s dashboard is hosted on an internal intranet

Noted that all IP addresses were from the 192.168.x.x private range

Understood that access requires:

Internal network / VPN

Valid authentication

2️⃣ Identifying Normal User Behavior

Using the reference PDF, I identified the expected flow:

401 Unauthorized

/login page load

POST /login

Dashboard resources (CSS, JS)

Limited, irregular API requests

This represents human-driven interaction.

3️⃣ Spotting Suspicious Activity

I looked for:

Long sequences of API requests

Requests made at regular time intervals

API calls without dashboard refresh

Repeated access to multiple factories and machines

➡️ This pattern suggests automation or scripting, not normal user behavior.

4️⃣ Identifying the Suspicious User

One user ID stood out due to:

Activity spanning multiple days

High-frequency API requests

Consistent timing patterns

Broad access across factories

🚨 Findings
❌ Internet-Based Attack

The breach could NOT have happened directly from the internet.

Reason:

Dashboard is not internet-facing

Only accessible from Daikibo’s internal network

Credentials alone are insufficient without network access

⚠️ Suspicious User Identified

User ID:

dBCm2JjBU815PB8zPDvKqv


Why this user is suspicious:

Appears across multiple sessions and dates

Shows automated-like API polling behavior

Requests machine data more frequently than normal users

Activity does not align with expected dashboard usage

📝 Quiz Answers
Q1:

Is there a way for a hacker to access Daikibo's manufacturing status dashboard directly from the internet?

✅ Answer:

No, the attacker has no direct access to the status dashboard.

Q2:

Looking at the web_requests.log, what is the user ID with the most suspicious activity?

✅ Answer:

dBCm2JjBU815PB8zPDvKqv

🧩 Key Skills Demonstrated

Log analysis

Threat detection

Identifying automated behavior

Understanding internal network security

Cybersecurity investigation mindset

📈 Outcome

Successfully identified abnormal activity using log analysis

Determined attack constraints based on network architecture

Demonstrated real-world cybersecurity investigation skills aligned with Deloitte workflows

