Datacom Cybersecurity Job Simulation::
Task 1 & Task 2 – Security Analysis & Risk Assessment
📌 Overview
This repository documents my completion of the Datacom Cybersecurity Job Simulation, where I worked through realistic cybersecurity scenarios focused on incident analysis, business impact assessment, and risk-based security decision making.

The simulation is divided into two key tasks:

Task 1: Incident investigation and breach impact analysis

Task 2: Organisational cybersecurity risk assessment

🎯 Learning Objectives

Through these tasks, I developed practical experience in:

Analysing real-world cyber incidents

Identifying vulnerabilities and attack vectors

Assessing legal, financial, and reputational impact

Performing structured cybersecurity risk assessments

Communicating findings clearly in a professional format

🔴 Task 1: Introduction to Cyber Security
Incident Investigation & Impact Assessment
🏢 Client Background

Orion Health Services

Mid-sized healthcare technology provider

~250 employees

Operates across Australia and New Zealand

Manages sensitive patient and employee data

Provides cloud-based software to healthcare clinics

🚨 Incident Summary

Incident Type: Ransomware attack

Detection:

Unusual outbound traffic from an internal server

Employees locked out of systems

Ransom note discovered on a shared drive

🔓 Attack Analysis
Initial Entry Point

Phishing email sent to a finance team member

Contained a malicious Excel attachment

Likely relied on macro execution or embedded malware

Attack Progression

Phishing email opened

Malware executed on endpoint

Credential harvesting using Mimikatz

Lateral movement across systems

Ransomware deployed and files encrypted

📂 Compromised Data

Employee payroll records

Patient appointment schedules

Internal system credentials

💻 Systems Affected

File server

HR systems

Finance systems

Backup server (partially encrypted)

🚩 Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)

Suspicious login from an overseas IP address

Use of Mimikatz credential-dumping tool

Files encrypted with .orionlock extension

📉 Business Impact
Legal & Regulatory

Potential healthcare data protection violations

Mandatory breach notification obligations

Financial

Operational downtime

Incident response and recovery costs

Potential ransom exposure

Reputational

Loss of trust from healthcare clients

Damage to brand credibility

🛡️ Key Recommendations

Improve phishing detection and email security

Enforce Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)

Deploy Endpoint Detection & Response (EDR)

Isolate and protect backup infrastructure

Conduct regular security awareness training

🟠 Task 2: Cybersecurity Risk Assessment
RetailNova Pty Ltd
🏢 Client Overview

RetailNova Pty Ltd

Headquartered in Melbourne, Australia

~1,200 employees

~$450 million annual revenue

85 physical stores + e-commerce platform

Uses AWS, Salesforce (CRM), SAP (ERP), cloud POS systems

RetailNova handles large volumes of customer PII, loyalty data, and tokenised payment data, making cybersecurity a critical business requirement.

🎯 Task Objective

To conduct a structured cybersecurity risk assessment by:

Identifying critical assets

Analysing threats and vulnerabilities

Assessing likelihood and impact

Prioritising risks

Recommending mitigations

🛠️ Risk Assessment Methodology

Asset-based risk identification

Threat and vulnerability analysis

Likelihood and consequence scoring

Inherent vs residual risk evaluation

Risk prioritisation and ownership

🚨 Key Risks Identified
🔴 Risk 1: Phishing-Based Credential Compromise

Assets at Risk: Customer data, CRM, internal systems

Inherent Risk: HIGH

Residual Risk: HIGH

Cause: Human error and frequent phishing attempts

🟠 Risk 2: Third-Party Vendor Data Exposure

Assets at Risk: Customer email and loyalty data

Inherent Risk: HIGH

Residual Risk: MEDIUM

Cause: Limited visibility into vendor security controls

🟠 Risk 3: Malware Introduction via BYOD Devices

Assets at Risk: AWS systems, POS infrastructure

Inherent Risk: HIGH

Residual Risk: MEDIUM

Cause: Inconsistent endpoint security on personal devices

🛡️ Recommended Mitigations

Mandatory Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)

Endpoint Detection & Response (EDR)

Regular phishing simulations

Strengthened third-party risk management

BYOD device compliance enforcement

Network segmentation

🧠 Skills Demonstrated

Cyber incident analysis

Ransomware attack understanding

Cybersecurity risk assessment

Threat and vulnerability identification

Business impact analysis

Professional cybersecurity documentation

📈 Outcome

This simulation strengthened my ability to:

Analyse real-world cybersecurity incidents

Translate technical findings into business impact

Prioritise cybersecurity risks using structured frameworks

Communicate security findings clearly for stakeholders

